WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.320
Hi, I'm Quince!

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.381
AgentJev picks between an agent's options.

00:00:04.381 --> 00:00:07.815
Here's how it ignores their order, yet lets them talk.

00:00:10.642 --> 00:00:14.320
Encode the shared state once, give each option a private branch, then

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.692
let options meet only in a small head with no positions.

00:00:20.342 --> 00:00:23.054
The state and the question are encoded once and cached.

00:00:25.377 --> 00:00:28.138
Each option gets its own copy of that cache.

00:00:28.138 --> 00:00:31.819
No option sees another, and every one starts at the same position.

00:00:32.239 --> 00:00:34.604
Each branch comes out as one vector.

00:00:34.604 --> 00:00:39.334
Only now do the options meet, in a two-layer transformer with no positional embeddings.

00:00:39.754 --> 00:00:42.067
A scorer reads one number per option.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:45.041
Nothing anywhere records which slot an option arrived in.

00:00:46.842 --> 00:00:48.734
The repository's own figure.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:54.883
Without sharing, all sixty-four options recompute the state: over thirty-three thousand backbone tokens.

00:00:55.303 --> 00:00:59.703
Shared, about two and a half thousand: exactly ninety-two point four percent fewer.

00:00:59.703 --> 00:01:02.749
On the clock, two point oh four times faster.

00:01:04.192 --> 00:01:07.443
The set head's output is added onto each option's own vector.

00:01:07.863 --> 00:01:10.060
The first term is each option, read alone.

00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:13.371
The second is what knowing the rest of the set adds.

00:01:14.345 --> 00:01:17.346
Zero the second term, and it's a plain per-option scorer.

00:01:18.692 --> 00:01:22.927
Shuffle the list: across two thousand five hundred and twenty permutations, no

00:01:22.927 --> 00:01:26.810
answer changed, and no logit moved past the float's last bits.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.724
Change which other options are on it, and a logit moves a

00:01:30.724 --> 00:01:32.762
median of zero point zero eight eight.

00:01:32.762 --> 00:01:33.635
The options interact.

00:01:35.142 --> 00:01:39.340
Isolate options in the backbone, let them meet in a head without

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.788
positions: order carries nothing, content still counts.

00:01:43.692 --> 00:01:48.652
To recap: a shared prefix, private branches, and a position-free head where options meet.

00:01:49.072 --> 00:01:51.182
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:51.182 --> 00:01:51.784
I'm Quince.

00:01:51.784 --> 00:01:52.086
Bye!
